  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 1234 PM MDT Thu Aug 20 2026\n\nModels in good agreement through the extended period with\npersistent monsoonal moisture moving across the Rockies.\n\nSaturday through Wednesday...persistent high pressure will sit\nacross the Rockies with near daily, upper disturbances moving\noverhead. Saturday looks like a down day, with mostly isolated\nto scattered shower and thunderstorm activity across Colorado. \nAs we move into Sunday and Monday, two strong embedded upper \nwaves will track southeast across Colorado. Each will bring a \nround of widespread thunderstorms and heavy rainfall for most of\nsouthern Colorado. The flash flood risk will be elevated both \ndays on area burn scars. Moving into next week, several waves \nwill move across Colorado, each generating daily afternoon and \nevening thunderstorms across the Mountains, spreading southeast \ninto the adjacent Plains. Overall, temperatures will remain hot,\nwith upper 80s to upper 90s across the Plains.",
